  ('latest', 'published', 'Bryan Keeps Property Tax Rate at 62.4 Cents for Fiscal 2027', '<p>BRYAN — Bryan''s city property tax rate will stay at $0.624 per $100 of taxable value for the 2027 fiscal year after the City Council gave final approval to the tax rate ordinance at a special meeting Sept. 15, the city said.</p><img src="/sites/breakingbcs/photos/bcs2-ln-03.webp" alt="Buildings in the Downtown Bryan Historic District (file photo, 2009). Photo: Billy Hathorn / Wikimedia Commons (CC BY-SA 2.5)"><p><em>▲ Buildings in the Downtown Bryan Historic District (file photo, 2009). Photo: Billy Hathorn / Wikimedia Commons (CC BY-SA 2.5)</em></p><p>The rate has been unchanged since fiscal 2023, when it was lowered, and the city said it has not raised its rate since fiscal 1999. The new fiscal year began Oct. 1.</p><p>Because property values are rising, the same rate still means a slightly larger bill for many homeowners. The city''s required tax rate notice puts the average taxable homestead value at $311,402, up from $306,495 last year, and estimates the city''s portion of the tax on that home at $1,943.15, an increase of about $30.</p><p>The adopted rate is below both state benchmarks. The no-new-revenue rate, which would raise the same amount of tax from the same properties as last year, was calculated at about 67.2 cents, and the voter-approval rate, the highest rate the city could adopt without an election, at about 63 cents, according to the city''s notices.</p><p>"At a time when tax rates are going up for many across the country, we''re choosing stability for our residents in Bryan," Mayor Bobby Gutierrez said in the city''s announcement.</p><p>About 80% of the expected property tax revenue will go to the general fund, which pays for services such as police, fire, parks, libraries and street repairs, the city said. The remaining 20% goes to debt service and the city''s tax increment reinvestment zones, special districts that set aside tax growth for development in certain areas.</p><p>Final tax bills also include school district and county taxes, and property values are set each year by the Brazos Central Appraisal District. The city''s full fiscal 2027 budget is available on its website, at the city secretary''s office and at Clara B. Mounce Public Library.</p><p><em>※ This article was written with the help of AI, based on public and official sources.</em></p>', 'The Bryan City Council gave final approval Sept. 15 to keeping the city tax rate at $0.624 per $100 of value. The average homestead''s city tax bill is projected to rise about $30.', '/sites/breakingbcs/photos/bcs2-ln-03.webp', '2026-09-16T14:10:00-05:00'::timestamptz, array['Bryan','property tax','city budget','Bryan City Council','fiscal 2027']::text[], '• 확인할 점: The Aug. 27 tax rate notice lists the total levy on all properties falling from $64,207,048 to $60,657,765 (-5.53%), while the Sept. 15 agenda ratified a ''property tax revenue increase'' in the budget. These conflict; the levy figures were left out. Ask the city if needed.
• 확인할 점: The mayor''s quote mentions 28 fiscal years without an increase; the release text says since FY1999. Kept the release wording.
• 확인할 점: The tax rate notice recorded Council Member Ray Arrington (SMD 2) absent for the August vote to propose the rate; the Sept. 15 final vote count was not found and is not stated.
• 확인할 점: Total FY2027 budget amount not given in sources read; omitted.
• 확인할 점: File photo license: GFDL / CC BY-SA 2.5,2.0,1.0 (self, Billy Hathorn); CC BY-SA 2.5 chosen.
• 원문(City of Bryan — City of Bryan Property Tax Rate to Remain Steady (Sept. 16, 2026)): https://www.bryantx.gov/news/posts/city-of-bryan-property-tax-rate-to-remain-steady/
• 원문(City of Bryan — Notice of Meeting to Vote on Tax Rate (Aug. 27, 2026)): https://www.bryantx.gov/news/posts/notice-of-meeting-to-vote-on-tax-rate/
• 원문(City of Bryan — Taxpayer Impact Statement for Fiscal Year 2026-2027 (Aug. 18, 2026)): https://www.bryantx.gov/news/posts/city-of-bryan-taxpayer-impact-statement-for-fiscal-year-2026-2027/
• 원문(City of Bryan — Behind the Gavel: Sept. 15, 2026 Special Meeting (Sept. 9, 2026)): https://www.bryantx.gov/news/posts/behind-the-gavel-sept-15-2026-special-meeting/
• 이용 조건: Text: facts from City of Bryan releases and public notices, rewritten; one quote from the release / Photo: CC BY-SA 2.5, Billy Hathorn, File:Downtown Bryan, TX, Historic District IMG 1026.JPG
