  ('basketball', 'published', 'Alabama Transfer Essence Cody to Sit Out Aggies'' 2026-27 Season', '<p>COLLEGE STATION — Texas A&amp;M women''s basketball senior Essence Cody, a transfer from Alabama, will not play in the 2026-27 season, she announced Monday. Cody said she is expecting her first child in January.</p><img src="/sites/breakingbcs/photos/bcs2-sp-07.webp" alt="Basketballs on a ball rack (file photo, 2018; not taken at Texas A&amp;M). Photo: Todd Greene / Unsplash"><p><em>▲ Basketballs on a ball rack (file photo, 2018; not taken at Texas A&amp;M). Photo: Todd Greene / Unsplash</em></p><p>"Becoming a mother is the biggest blessing of my life," Cody said in a statement published by Texas A&amp;M Athletics. She said she plans to lead from the sideline this season and added, "I will be the loudest voice on our bench all year." Cody plans to return for the 2027-28 season.</p><p>Cody played in 94 games over three seasons at Alabama and started six NCAA Tournament games during three tournament trips, according to the athletics department. She averaged 11.5 points, 5.7 rebounds and 1.6 blocks and shot 51.5% from the field.</p><p>"We are incredibly proud of Essence," head coach Joni Taylor said. "She has handled everything with grace and we know she is going to be an incredible mother." Taylor said Cody''s leadership "will be pivotal for us this season."</p><p>Taylor, in her fifth season at Texas A&amp;M, said when practice opened in September that this year''s team is guard-led and "we are definitely playing faster."</p><p>The Aggies will appear on national television 10 times this season, the SEC and ESPN announced last week. The first is the Nov. 5 home game against Louisiana on SEC Network. Nonconference road games at Cal on Dec. 3, in the SEC/ACC Challenge, and at Nebraska on Dec. 12 will air on ACC Network and Big Ten Network.</p><p>Seven SEC games are set for SEC Network: LSU on Jan. 7, Vanderbilt on Jan. 14, Texas on Jan. 21 and Feb. 14, Oklahoma on Jan. 31, South Carolina on Feb. 11 and Georgia on Feb. 22. Texas A&amp;M opens the season against Arkansas-Pine Bluff at 7 p.m. Nov. 2 at Reed Arena.</p><p><em>※ This article was written with the help of AI, based on public and official sources.</em></p>', 'Senior transfer Essence Cody, who played three seasons at Alabama, will sit out her first year at Texas A&M because she is expecting her first child in January. She plans to return in 2027-28.', '/sites/breakingbcs/photos/bcs2-sp-07.webp', '2026-10-12T16:10:00-05:00'::timestamptz, array['Texas A&M women''s basketball','Essence Cody','Joni Taylor','SEC Network','Reed Arena']::text[], '• 확인할 점: Personal news (pregnancy) was announced publicly by the player herself through Texas A&M Athletics; the story uses only what she shared. Editor may prefer a lighter headline.
• 확인할 점: TV list is from the Oct. 7 ESPN/SEC release as posted by Texas A&M; the release says 10 national TV games, and the games it names add up to 10.
• 원문(Texas A&M Athletics — Cody to Sit Out 2026-27 Season (Oct. 12, 2026)): https://12thman.com/news/2026/10/12/cody-to-sit-out-2026-27-season
• 원문(Texas A&M Athletics — Women''s Hoops Lands 10 National TV Games (Oct. 7, 2026)): https://12thman.com/news/2026/10/7/womens-hoops-lands-10-national-tv-games
• 원문(Texas A&M Athletics — Taylor Meets Media as Aggies Open Practice (Sept. 21, 2026)): https://12thman.com/news/2026/09/21/taylor-meets-media-as-aggies-open-practice
• 이용 조건: Text: facts from Texas A&M Athletics (12thman.com) releases, rewritten; quotes as published by the athletics department / Photo: Unsplash License, Todd Greene / Unsplash, https://unsplash.com/photos/wilson-basketball-on-rack-9geJ0hPetUM
• 발행: 대표님 요청으로 승인 대기 없이 바로 발행'),
  ('business', 'published', 'College Station Asks Residents Which Stores They Want to See Next', '<p>COLLEGE STATION — College Station is asking residents to name the store or shopping brand they would most like to see open in the city, part of a quarterly survey run by its economic development team.</p><img src="/sites/breakingbcs/photos/bcs2-bz-04.webp" alt="Shoppers walk through a shopping arcade in Melbourne, Australia (file photo, 2016). It was not taken in College Station. Photo: Heidi Fin / Unsplash"><p><em>▲ Shoppers walk through a shopping arcade in Melbourne, Australia (file photo, 2016). It was not taken in College Station. Photo: Heidi Fin / Unsplash</em></p><p>The question is this quarter''s topic for Shape College Station, a short community survey led by Grow College Station, the city''s economic development office, the city said in an Oct. 12 news release. The survey is open through Nov. 30 and takes less than a minute, according to the city.</p><p>Grow College Station uses the answers as current local data when it talks with retailers, developers and site selectors, the city said. When a brand considers a new market, evidence of local demand is part of its business case.</p><p>"Every time a resident drives to Houston or Austin to shop, that''s convenience and revenue leaving College Station," Chief Development Officer Michael Ostrowski said in the release.</p><p>The city noted that it does not decide which businesses open in College Station. Retailers make those decisions based on their own market studies, but resident input helps shape the city''s recruitment priorities, according to the release.</p><p>The city ties local retail to its budget: sales tax revenue helps pay for city services. In September, the City Council approved land-sale and incentive agreements for a Bass Pro Shops store and a neighboring mixed-use project in the Midtown area.</p><p>Grow College Station plans to compile responses after the survey closes and share results in December on its website and the city''s social media channels, the city said. Each quarter the survey poses a new question about restaurants, shops and attractions.</p><p><em>※ This article was written with the help of AI, based on public and official sources.</em></p>', 'College Station''s quarterly Shape College Station survey asks residents which store or shopping brand they want in town. It is open through Nov. 30, with results due in December.', '/sites/breakingbcs/photos/bcs2-bz-04.webp', '2026-10-13T09:45:00-05:00'::timestamptz, array['College Station','retail','economic development','survey']::text[], '• 확인할 점: Survey closes Nov. 30; results promised in December — follow-up story possible.
• 확인할 점: We omitted the survey web address per style rules.
• 확인할 점: Commons file is 576 x 848 px (meets 500px minimum); satellite image dated 2006.
• 원문(Grow College Station / City of College Station — Quarterly survey asks which stores or brands residents want to see in College Station (Oct. 12, 2026)): https://grow.cstx.gov/news/posts/quarterly-survey-asks-which-stores-or-brands-residents-want-to-see-in-college-station/
