  ('aggie-football', 'published', 'Olano, White Named Midseason All-Americans; Saka, Hicks on Lombardi List', '<p>COLLEGE STATION — Texas A&amp;M''s kicking specialists, David Olano and Tyler White, were named to midseason All-America teams by The Associated Press and Sports Illustrated on Thursday, Texas A&amp;M Athletics said.</p><img src="/sites/breakingbcs/photos/bcs2-sp-03.webp" alt="The exterior of Kyle Field at Texas A&amp;M University in College Station (file photo, 2022). Photo: David Rodezno / Unsplash"><p><em>▲ The exterior of Kyle Field at Texas A&amp;M University in College Station (file photo, 2022). Photo: David Rodezno / Unsplash</em></p><p>White, the Aggies'' punter, made the AP first team and the SI second team. Olano, the place-kicker, was an SI first-team pick and made the AP second team.</p><p>Through six games, White led the nation with an average of 50.4 yards per punt, according to the athletics department. He had 14 punts of 50 yards or more, including a career-long 72-yarder at Missouri, and only nine of his 24 punts had been returned, for an average of 1.8 yards. He was named the Ray Guy Award''s punter of the week on Sept. 28.</p><p>Olano made all nine of his field goal tries and all 19 extra-point kicks in the first half of the season. The school said he was the first Aggie kicker to make his first nine kicks of a season since Todd Pegram made his first 12 in 2004. He had made four field goals of 50 yards or more, tied for the most in the country, including a career-long 57-yarder against Arkansas that earned him SEC Special Teams Player of the Week honors.</p><p>On Wednesday, the Rotary Club of Houston and the Lombardi Award committee put two Texas A&amp;M defenders, Anto Saka and DJ Hicks, on the award''s midseason watch list. Hicks had 12 tackles, 1.5 tackles for loss, half a sack and three quarterback hurries at the halfway point, and Saka had 10 tackles, 2.0 tackles for loss, half a sack, three hurries and a fumble recovery, the athletics department said.</p><p>Texas A&amp;M, 3-3 after a loss at Missouri, hosts The Citadel at noon Saturday at Kyle Field. The game will stream on SEC Network+.</p><p><em>※ This article was written with the help of AI, based on public and official sources.</em></p>', 'Texas A&M kicker David Olano and punter Tyler White made the AP and Sports Illustrated midseason All-America teams, and defenders Anto Saka and DJ Hicks joined the Lombardi Award watch list.', '/sites/breakingbcs/photos/bcs2-sp-03.webp', '2026-10-15T16:30:00-05:00'::timestamptz, array['Texas A&M football','David Olano','Tyler White','All-America','Lombardi Award']::text[], '• 확인할 점: Stats are as of the midseason releases (Oct. 14-15); Olano and White numbers have since changed (later releases: Olano 13-for-13, White 49.4 average after Alabama).
• 확인할 점: Releases do not give Saka''s and Hicks'' positions, so they are called ''defenders'' (stats are defensive).
• 원문(Texas A&M Athletics — Olano and White Earn Multiple Midseason All-America Honors (Oct. 15, 2026)): https://12thman.com/news/2026/10/15/olano-and-white-named-ap-midseason-all-americans
• 원문(Texas A&M Athletics — Saka and Hicks Named to Lombardi Award Midseason Watch List (Oct. 14, 2026)): https://12thman.com/news/2026/10/14/saka-and-hicks-named-to-lombardi-award-midseason-watch-list
• 원문(Texas A&M Athletics — Football Drops 27-6 Decision to No. 14 Missouri (Oct. 10, 2026)): https://12thman.com/news/2026/10/10/aggies-at-missouri
