  ('college-station', 'published', 'College Station Christmas Parade Entries Due Nov. 6; Park Lights Start Nov. 26', '<p>COLLEGE STATION — Community groups, schools, businesses and residents who want a place in this year''s College Station Christmas Parade have until Friday, Nov. 6, to register, the city said.</p><img src="/sites/breakingbcs/photos/bcs2-cv-06.webp" alt="Holiday lights on trees at Vitruvian Park in Addison, Texas (file photo, 2022). It is not College Station&#x27;s Christmas in the Park or parade. Photo: Bryan Dickerson / Unsplash"><p><em>▲ Holiday lights on trees at Vitruvian Park in Addison, Texas (file photo, 2022). It is not College Station''s Christmas in the Park or parade. Photo: Bryan Dickerson / Unsplash</em></p><p>The parade steps off at 4 p.m. Saturday, Dec. 5, according to the city''s Public Communications office, which opened registration in late September. Every registered participant must attend a mandatory meeting Nov. 16, where line-up details, parade rules and instructions will be provided, the city said.</p><p>The route begins at Post Oak Mall and heads west on Holleman Drive, then turns south on Dartmouth Street, the city said. It crosses Southwest Parkway, turns east on Krenek Tap Road and ends at Stephen C. Beachy Central Park.</p><p>An untimed 1.5-mile Jingle Bell Fun Run for runners, walkers and strollers starts at 3 p.m. the same day, ahead of the parade, and finishes at Christmas in the Park, according to the city''s holiday events page.</p><p>The park''s Christmas in the Park display of more than 1 million lights will be on from 6 to 11 p.m. nightly from Nov. 26 through Jan. 1, the city said. A Christmas in the Park event is planned from 6 to 10 p.m. Dec. 5.</p><p>The light display began in 1984, when a local family paid for a couple of light panels, and has grown into a holiday tradition, according to the city.</p><p><em>※ This article was written with the help of AI, based on public and official sources.</em></p>', 'Groups have until Nov. 6 to enter College Station''s Dec. 5 Christmas Parade. Christmas in the Park''s lights at Beachy Central Park will be on nightly from Nov. 26 through Jan. 1.', '/sites/breakingbcs/photos/bcs2-cv-06.webp', '2026-10-23T10:15:00-05:00'::timestamptz, array['College Station','Christmas parade','Christmas in the Park','holiday events','Beachy Central Park']::text[], '• 확인할 점: Parade registration release dated Sept. 29, 2026; holiday schedule from the city''s ''A College Station Christmas'' page (undated, read Oct. 27, 2026). The page gives dates without a year; assumed 2026-27 season. Confirm.
• 확인할 점: Nov. 16 meeting time/place not given.
• 확인할 점: Road closures for the parade not yet announced; the separate Dartmouth-Krenek Tap intersection work (another writer''s road beat) was not checked against the parade date.
• 확인할 점: Parade webpage URL left out of body per style.
• 원문(City of College Station — Registration for the College Station Christmas Parade is underway! (Sept. 29, 2026)): https://www.cstx.gov/news/posts/registration-for-the-college-station-christmas-parade-is-underway/
• 원문(City of College Station blog — Spread holiday cheer: Registration for the College Station Christmas Parade is underway (Sept. 29, 2026)): https://blog.cstx.gov/2026/09/29/spread-holiday-cheer-registration-for-the-college-station-christmas-parade-is-underway/
• 원문(City of College Station — A College Station Christmas event page (read Oct. 27, 2026)): https://www.cstx.gov/parks-recreation-culture/events/community-events/a-college-station-christmas/
• 이용 조건: Text: facts from City of College Station releases, rewritten / Photo: Unsplash License, Bryan Dickerson / Unsplash, https://unsplash.com/photos/a-colorful-display-of-trees-and-lights-reflecting-in-the-water-0rjagDlvXQg
