  ('bryan', 'published', 'Bryan Sets Holiday Magic for Dec. 3, Historic Porch Stroll for Dec. 13', '<p>BRYAN — The City of Bryan has posted dates for its December traditions, including the 28th Holiday Magic celebration and a self-guided walk past decorated homes in one of the city''s oldest neighborhoods.</p><img src="/sites/breakingbcs/photos/bcs2-cv-04.webp" alt="A historic two-story frame home with a front porch (file photo; location not given, not in Bryan and not decorated for the holidays). Photo: Roger Starnes Sr / Unsplash"><p><em>▲ A historic two-story frame home with a front porch (file photo; location not given, not in Bryan and not decorated for the holidays). Photo: Roger Starnes Sr / Unsplash</em></p><p>Holiday Magic is scheduled from 5:30 to 8:30 p.m. Thursday, Dec. 3, at Sue Haswell Memorial Park, according to the city''s event page. Admission, activities, parking and the shuttle are free, and pets are not allowed, the city said.</p><p>Planned activities include photos with Santa and holiday characters, snow hills, train rides, inflatables, face painting, arts and crafts, a scavenger hunt, letters to Santa, hot chocolate and cookies, and performances by Bryan ISD choirs. Food vendors will also be on site.</p><p>The Holiday Porch Stroll is set for 4 to 7 p.m. Sunday, Dec. 13. Visitors start at Heritage Park and then walk through the East Side Historic District, viewing the exteriors of historic homes decorated for the season, the city said.</p><p>The East Side Historic District is listed on the National Register of Historic Places, the federal list of places considered worthy of preservation.</p><p>The city''s parks department also runs Reindeer on the Run, in which clues posted from Nov. 30 through Dec. 14 lead families to nine reindeer figures hidden in Bryan parks and city buildings. Participants who report finding all nine are entered in a prize drawing, according to the city.</p><p><em>※ This article was written with the help of AI, based on public and official sources.</em></p>', 'Bryan''s 28th Holiday Magic is Dec. 3 at Sue Haswell Memorial Park, and the Holiday Porch Stroll through the East Side Historic District is Dec. 13, the city''s event pages show.', '/sites/breakingbcs/photos/bcs2-cv-04.webp', '2026-10-25T13:30:00-05:00'::timestamptz, array['Bryan','Holiday Magic','historic preservation','East Side Historic District','holiday events']::text[], '• 확인할 점: Dates from the city''s special-event pages (read Oct. 27, 2026): Holiday Magic page says ''returning for its 28th year on Thursday, Dec. 3''; Porch Stroll page is headed ''2026''. Dec. 3, 2026 is a Thursday and Dec. 13, 2026 a Sunday, consistent.
• 확인할 점: Reindeer on the Run page gives ''Nov. 30 through Dec. 14'' without a year; assumed current. Confirm before publication.
• 확인할 점: Parking locations/shuttle stops for 2026 Holiday Magic not yet posted (2025 used Blinn College lots) — left out.
• 확인할 점: NRHP status of the East Side Historic District is taken from the Commons file page of a contributing property (Hudson-Harrison House, listed Sept. 25, 1987); the National Register definition is from Bryan''s Feb. 19, 2026 downtown release. Not checked on NPS directly.
• 확인할 점: Photo is a private residence; no address given in caption beyond street name. Editor may prefer to drop the street name.
• 원문(City of Bryan — Holiday Magic event page (read Oct. 27, 2026)): https://www.bryantx.gov/special-events/holiday-magic/
• 원문(City of Bryan — Holiday Porch Stroll event page (read Oct. 27, 2026)): https://www.bryantx.gov/special-events/holiday-porch-stroll/
• 원문(City of Bryan — Reindeer on the Run event page (read Oct. 27, 2026)): https://www.bryantx.gov/special-events/reindeer-on-the-run/
• 원문(Wikimedia Commons — Hudson-Harrison House file description (NRHP East Side Historic District)): https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hudson_harrison_house_bryan_tx_2014.jpg
• 원문(City of Bryan — Historic Downtown Bryan Earns National Designation (Feb. 19, 2026)): https://www.bryantx.gov/news/posts/historic-downtown-bryan-earns-national-designation/
• 이용 조건: Text: facts from City of Bryan public pages, rewritten / Photo: Unsplash License, Roger Starnes Sr / Unsplash, https://unsplash.com/photos/a-house-with-a-porch-and-a-covered-porch-VRw302FdHfU
