  ('sports', 'published', 'Freshman Ireland Churchill Makes National List as Aggie Soccer Nears Finale', '<p>COLLEGE STATION — Texas A&amp;M soccer freshman Ireland Churchill was ranked No. 17 on Top Drawer Soccer''s midseason Top 100 list, released over the weekend, Texas A&amp;M Athletics said Monday.</p><img src="/sites/breakingbcs/photos/bcs2-sp-10.webp" alt="A soccer ball on a grass field in front of a goal (file photo, 2018; taken in Germany, not at Texas A&amp;M&#x27;s Ellis Field). Photo: Markus Spiske / Unsplash"><p><em>▲ A soccer ball on a grass field in front of a goal (file photo, 2018; taken in Germany, not at Texas A&amp;M''s Ellis Field). Photo: Markus Spiske / Unsplash</em></p><p>Churchill, from Eastvale, California, has 11 goals and 25 points this season, both third in the Southeastern Conference, according to the athletics department. She also ranks third in conference-only games with six goals and 13 points in nine SEC matches.</p><p>She is the first Aggie to reach double-digit goals in a season since Liz Keester in 2013, the school said, and her 11 goals tie her for sixth among Texas A&amp;M freshmen. She has scored twice in a game four times, three of them in SEC play.</p><p>Her latest two-goal game came Thursday in a 3-2 loss at Missouri. Churchill scored in the fifth and seventh minutes, finishing off plays that began with long free kicks, to give Texas A&amp;M a 2-0 lead. The athletics department said it was the second-fastest that an Aggie has scored twice in a game, behind Ashlee Pistorius in the first six minutes of a 2007 NCAA Tournament win over Stephen F. Austin.</p><p>Missouri tied the game before halftime and scored the winner on a header 59 seconds into the second half. Texas A&amp;M started eight freshmen, its most in a game since 1993, according to the release.</p><p>The loss left the Aggies 4-11-1 overall and 0-8-1 in the SEC. Texas A&amp;M ends its season at noon Sunday, Nov. 1, against Ole Miss at Ellis Field. The match is the team''s Senior Day.</p><p><em>※ This article was written with the help of AI, based on public and official sources.</em></p>', 'Texas A&M freshman Ireland Churchill, third in the SEC with 11 goals, is No. 17 on a national midseason top-100 list. The Aggies close their season Sunday against Ole Miss at Ellis Field.', '/sites/breakingbcs/photos/bcs2-sp-10.webp', '2026-10-27T09:10:00-05:00'::timestamptz, array['Texas A&M soccer','Ireland Churchill','Ellis Field','SEC soccer']::text[], '• 확인할 점: Top Drawer Soccer is a private outlet; its ranking is reported only as stated in the Texas A&M release.
• 확인할 점: Photo is a generic public-domain college soccer image (Navy vs. Drexel, 2003) because no freely licensed photo of Texas A&M soccer or Ellis Field was found on Commons; caption says it is not Texas A&M.
• 확인할 점: Release says ''Stephen F. Austin'' as ''SFA''; spelled out in story.
• 확인할 점: The release says Sunday''s match ''wraps up the 2026 campaign''; SEC Tournament qualification is not discussed in the release.
• 원문(Texas A&M Athletics — Churchill Named to Top Drawer Soccer Top Freshman List (Oct. 26, 2026)): https://12thman.com/news/2026/10/26/churchill-named-to-top-drawer-soccer-top-freshman-list
• 원문(Texas A&M Athletics — Aggies Edged Out by Missouri, 3-2 (Oct. 23, 2026)): https://12thman.com/news/2026/10/23/aggies-edged-out-by-missouri-3-2
• 이용 조건: Text: facts from Texas A&M Athletics (12thman.com) releases, rewritten / Photo: Unsplash License, Markus Spiske / Unsplash, https://unsplash.com/photos/white-and-black-soccer-ball-KWQ2kQtxiKE
• 발행: 대표님 요청으로 승인 대기 없이 바로 발행'),
  ('fashion', 'published', 'Aggie Ring Day Nov. 6: Comfortable Shoes and Weather-Ready Layers Advised', '<p>COLLEGE STATION — Texas A&amp;M students receiving their Aggie Rings next week will want to think about their shoes as much as their outfits. The Association of Former Students, the university''s alumni organization, will hold Aggie Ring Day on Friday, Nov. 6, from 9 a.m. to 6 p.m. at the Clayton W. Williams Jr. Alumni Center.</p><img src="/sites/breakingbcs/photos/bcs2-ls-07.webp" alt="Canvas sneakers on a sidewalk (file photo, 2023; not taken at Texas A&amp;M or on Aggie Ring Day). Photo: Valeriia Miller / Unsplash"><p><em>▲ Canvas sneakers on a sidewalk (file photo, 2023; not taken at Texas A&amp;M or on Aggie Ring Day). Photo: Valeriia Miller / Unsplash</em></p><p>The association''s guidance says Ring Day involves walking more than half a mile and advises recipients to wear shoes they can comfortably stand and walk in. It also suggests bringing water and considering personal fans or umbrellas, depending on the weather, and notes there is no indoor seating outside the building. Bags are allowed; balloons and animals other than service animals are not.</p><p>The weather is usually mild in early November. Federal climate normals for College Station''s Easterwood Field station show an average high of about 74 degrees and an average low of about 53 degrees on Nov. 6, so a morning group may start cool and an afternoon group may warm up. That spread makes a light layer that can be carried easily a practical choice.</p><p>Ring Day runs in 15-minute group time blocks shown on each recipient''s ticket, and the association says to expect thousands of people, long lines and long waits. There is no parking at the alumni center that day; shuttles run from the West Campus Garage, and Houston Street will be closed. Professional photographers will be in Aggie Park.</p><p>For those who would rather avoid the crowds or have mobility issues, the association is offering a Thursday, Nov. 5, pickup from 9 a.m. to 3 p.m. in 30-minute blocks, with limited spaces available first come, first served. Parking is available at the alumni center that day, and lines are expected to be short.</p><p>Recipients need their Aggie Ring ticket and at least two forms of identification from a list that includes the ring receipt, student ID, driver''s license or passport. Guests are not limited but may enter the building only with a ticketed recipient, and everyone must leave right after receiving rings. The association says lingering for photos inside or at Haynes Ring Plaza is not allowed that day, though people can return another day.</p><p>Then there is how to wear it. By tradition, students wear the ring with the class year facing them, a reminder that their time at Texas A&amp;M is not yet complete, according to the university. At commencement, the Association of Former Students leads graduates in turning their rings around to face the world. The association also suggests waiting several days before deciding on a resize, since hand size changes over the course of a day.</p><p><em>※ This article was written with the help of AI, based on public and official sources.</em></p>', 'Thousands of Aggies will pick up their rings Nov. 6 at the Williams Alumni Center. Organizers advise comfortable shoes for a walk of more than half a mile and planning for the weather.', '/sites/breakingbcs/photos/bcs2-ls-07.webp', '2026-10-27T10:05:00-05:00'::timestamptz, array['Aggie Ring Day','Texas A&M','traditions','what to wear']::text[], '• 확인할 점: Date, times and Thursday/Friday logistics from the Association of Former Students Ring Day page (aggienetwork.com/ring/ringday/) as of Oct. 27, 2026.
• 확인할 점: The Ring Day FAQ page mixes details from the October Ring Day (e.g., Oct. 8-10 parking and shuttle notes, Kyle Field photo hours). Only general FAQ items (shoes, water, fans/umbrellas, half-mile walk, bags, balloons, ID, guests, photos, resizing) were used. Check that FAQ items still apply to Nov. 6.
• 확인할 점: A KBTX report (not used as a source) mentioned more than 17,000 rings this year; not confirmed in an official source, so left out.
• 확인할 점: Temperature normals: NOAA NCEI 1991-2020 daily normals, station USW00003904 (Easterwood Field): Nov. 6 high 74.2, low 52.7. These are averages, not a forecast; editor may add the NWS forecast closer to the date.
• 확인할 점: The ''light layer'' line is service advice derived from the data; no brands named. The association''s guidance itself only addresses shoes.
• 확인할 점: Ring wearing tradition from tamu.edu Aggie Ring page. Hand (right ring finger) was mentioned only in a search summary of an AggieNetwork page and was not verified, so left out.
• 확인할 점: Photo: Commons file of the Williams Alumni Center, May 8, 2007; check for faces.
• 원문(The Association of Former Students — Aggie Ring Day (fall 2026 page)): https://www.aggienetwork.com/ring/ringday/
• 원문(The Association of Former Students — Aggie Ring Day FAQ): https://www.aggienetwork.com/ring/ringday/faq
• 원문(Texas A&M University — Aggie Ring tradition): https://www.tamu.edu/campus-community/traditions/aggie-culture/aggie-ring.html
• 원문(NOAA NCEI — U.S. Climate Normals 1991-2020, daily, station USW00003904 College Station): https://www.ncei.noaa.gov/access/services/data/v1?dataset=normals-daily-1991-2020&stations=USW00003904&format=csv&dataTypes=DLY-TMAX-NORMAL,DLY-TMIN-NORMAL&startDate=2010-11-04&endDate=2010-11-07
• 이용 조건: Text: original wording based on facts from The Association of Former Students and Texas A&M pages, and NOAA data (public domain) / Photo: Unsplash License, Valeriia Miller / Unsplash, https://unsplash.com/photos/a-persons-feet-wearing-brown-and-white-tennis-shoes-_D5aCBa1ygo
• 발행: 대표님 요청으로 승인 대기 없이 바로 발행'),
  ('latest', 'published', 'Bryan Police Urge 6-8 p.m. Trick-or-Treating, Slow Driving on Halloween', '<p>BRYAN — The Bryan Police Department is asking families to keep trick-or-treating between 6 and 8 p.m. on Halloween, which falls on Saturday this year, and is urging drivers to slow down while children are out.</p><img src="/sites/breakingbcs/photos/bcs2-ln-01.webp" alt="A lit jack-o&#x27;-lantern at night (file photo, 2022). It was not taken in Bryan. Photo: Alabama Extension / Wikimedia Commons (CC0 1.0)"><p><em>▲ A lit jack-o''-lantern at night (file photo, 2022). It was not taken in Bryan. Photo: Alabama Extension / Wikimedia Commons (CC0 1.0)</em></p><p>The recommended window gives officers a set period to focus on child safety and gives residents a consistent time to hand out treats, the City of Bryan said in a list of safety tips released Tuesday.</p><p>Police said moving vehicles are one of the biggest dangers to trick-or-treaters, because drivers can have trouble seeing children in dark costumes, especially around dusk. The department asked drivers to stay alert all evening.</p><p>For children and families, the department recommends that a parent or other responsible adult go along with young children, that everyone carry a flashlight, and that groups stay on well-lit streets and use sidewalks where possible. Children should cross at crosswalks or corners rather than zigzagging across the street, and should take off masks or anything else that blocks their view before crossing.</p><p>Police also advised visiting only homes with porch lights on, choosing costume props such as swords made of flexible material, and never eating unwrapped food or drinks. Tampering is rare, the department said, but parents should check treats and throw away anything suspicious or unwrapped. Parents are also encouraged to review the Texas Department of Public Safety sex offender registry for their area before going out.</p><p>Homeowners can help by turning on porch lights, clearing walkways, moving lit jack-o''-lanterns away from busy paths and using flashlights or LED candles instead of open flames. The city also suggested offering non-candy treats such as stickers or trading cards for children who cannot or do not want to eat candy.</p><p>Residents who see suspicious activity are asked to report it to the agency that covers the area: the Bryan Police Department or the Brazos County Sheriff''s Office, the College Station Police Department, or the Texas A&amp;M University Police Department.</p><p><em>※ This article was written with the help of AI, based on public and official sources.</em></p>', 'Bryan police recommend trick-or-treating from 6 to 8 p.m. on Halloween, adult supervision for young children and extra caution from drivers, who pose one of the biggest risks to children.', '/sites/breakingbcs/photos/bcs2-ln-01.webp', '2026-10-27T10:20:00-05:00'::timestamptz, array['Bryan','Bryan Police Department','Halloween','public safety','traffic safety']::text[], '• 확인할 점: The city release does not say whether the 6-8 p.m. window applies citywide by ordinance; it is written as a recommendation and described that way here.
• 확인할 점: Phone numbers for the agencies were in the release but left out per style rules.
• 확인할 점: The release names the ''Brazos County Sheriff''s Department''; the agency''s formal name is the Brazos County Sheriff''s Office, which is used here. Confirm the preferred name.
• 확인할 점: College Station police and Texas A&M police did not issue separate tips in the sources read; not included.
• 원문(City of Bryan — Trick-or-Treating Safety Tips (Oct. 27, 2026)): https://www.bryantx.gov/news/posts/trick-or-treating-safety-tips/
• 이용 조건: Text: facts from City of Bryan news release, rewritten / Photo: CC0 1.0, Alabama Extension, File:Jack-O-Lantern at night.jpg
• 발행: 대표님 요청으로 승인 대기 없이 바로 발행'),
  ('college-station', 'published', 'College Station''s CSTV Adds Free Streaming App Ahead of Halloween Movie Marathon', '<p>COLLEGE STATION — College Station''s government TV channel no longer requires a cable subscription to watch, and its long-running Halloween movie marathon returns this weekend.</p><img src="/sites/breakingbcs/photos/bcs2-cv-07.webp" alt="A lighted jack-o&#x27;-lantern Halloween decoration (file photo, 2017). It is not from CSTV&#x27;s movie marathon. Photo: Quilia / Unsplash"><p><em>▲ A lighted jack-o''-lantern Halloween decoration (file photo, 2017). It is not from CSTV''s movie marathon. Photo: Quilia / Unsplash</em></p><p>The city''s channel, recently rebranded as CSTV, is now available on CSTV+, a free streaming app for Roku, Fire TV, Apple TV, iOS and Android devices, the city''s Public Communications Department said in an Oct. 20 release. Cable subscribers can still find CSTV on Optimum Channel 19.</p><p>The app offers live and on-demand viewing of City Council and Planning and Zoning Commission meetings, the city''s podcast, community updates and event coverage, the city said. Live programming also streams on the city''s website, and on-demand videos are posted to the city''s YouTube channel.</p><p>The channel''s annual Halloween on 19 marathon of classic horror films starts Friday morning and runs through Saturday night, the city said Tuesday. Regular city programming about local projects, services and events will air between the movies.</p><p>This year''s lineup includes "Nosferatu" (1922), "Phantom of the Opera" (1925), "Little Shop of Horrors" (1960) and "The Last Man on Earth" (1964), according to the city.</p><p>The tradition began 17 years ago, when two videographers in the city''s Public Communications Department proposed airing older horror films before Halloween to draw more viewers to the government channel, the city said. The marathon is hosted on screen by "Grace Halloween," according to the city.</p><p><em>※ This article was written with the help of AI, based on public and official sources.</em></p>', 'College Station''s government channel, CSTV, is now on a free streaming app, CSTV+. Its 17-year-old Halloween classic-horror marathon airs from Friday morning through Saturday night.', '/sites/breakingbcs/photos/bcs2-cv-07.webp', '2026-10-27T11:30:00-05:00'::timestamptz, array['College Station','CSTV','Halloween','local government','streaming']::text[], '• 확인할 점: Film titles follow the city''s wording (''Phantom of the Opera'', ''Little Shop of Horrors''); the films'' official titles begin with ''The''.
• 확인할 점: Full film schedule/air times not checked (shown only as an image in the blog).
• 확인할 점: ''Grace Halloween'' is the on-screen host persona named in the city blog (blog byline ''By Grace Halloween''; news release by Grace Hallowell, Marketing Coordinator).
• 확인할 점: Photo: Nosferatu (1922) is public domain in the U.S. (published 1922); Commons tag PD-old.
• 원문(City of College Station — Stream CSTV, your local government channel, for free on your favorite devices (Oct. 20, 2026)): https://www.cstx.gov/news/posts/stream-cstv-your-local-government-channel-for-free-on-your-favorite-devices/
• 원문(City of College Station blog — Stream College Station''s local government channel for free (Oct. 20, 2026)): https://blog.cstx.gov/2026/10/20/stream-college-stations-local-government-channel-for-free-on-all-your-favorite-devices/
• 원문(City of College Station — Classic thrills, vintage chills: Catch our annual Halloween scare-a-thon on CSTV (Oct. 27, 2026)): https://blog.cstx.gov/2026/10/27/classic-thrills-vintage-chills-catch-our-annual-halloween-scare-a-thon-on-cstv/
• 이용 조건: Text: facts from City of College Station releases, rewritten / Photo: Unsplash License, Quilia / Unsplash, https://unsplash.com/photos/lighted-jack-o-lantern-ASNSoeead70
• 발행: 대표님 요청으로 승인 대기 없이 바로 발행'),
  ('business', 'published', 'Apartment Permits Push Bryan-College Station Housing Authorizations Up 86%', '<p>COLLEGE STATION — Builders in the College Station-Bryan metro area received permits for 3,254 new housing units in the first nine months of 2026, up about 86% from the same period last year, according to U.S. Census Bureau building permit data.</p><img src="/sites/breakingbcs/photos/bcs2-bz-02.webp" alt="A tower crane over a high-rise project in Austin (file photo, 2020; not in Bryan-College Station). Photo: Larry D. Moore / Wikimedia Commons (CC BY 4.0)"><p><em>▲ A tower crane over a high-rise project in Austin (file photo, 2020; not in Bryan-College Station). Photo: Larry D. Moore / Wikimedia Commons (CC BY 4.0)</em></p><p>The increase came almost entirely from larger apartment buildings. Permits through September covered 1,950 units in 16 buildings with five or more units each, compared with 176 units in one such building during the first nine months of 2025, the Census Bureau''s monthly metro reports show.</p><p>Single-family construction moved the other way. Local permit offices authorized 1,249 single-family homes from January through September, down about 10% from 1,384 a year earlier.</p><p>In September alone, the metro area authorized 527 units, including 403 units in one apartment building and 112 single-family homes. In September 2025, the total was 342 units, including 144 single-family homes.</p><p>The estimated construction value of all units authorized this year reached about $726.2 million, compared with about $371.9 million at the same point in 2025, according to the Census figures, which are reported in thousands of dollars.</p><p>The College Station-Bryan metro area includes Brazos, Burleson and Robertson counties. The Census Bureau counts housing units authorized by building permits, not construction starts or completions, and its monthly metro figures are not seasonally adjusted.</p><p>The numbers arrive as local officials plan for growth. In a September presentation to the College Station City Council, the city''s chief development officer said the active single-family and multifamily pipeline includes nearly 11,000 planned housing units.</p><p><em>※ This article was written with the help of AI, based on public and official sources.</em></p>', 'Census data show 3,254 housing units were authorized in the College Station-Bryan metro area through September, up from 1,746 a year earlier, as apartments surged and single-family permits slipped.', '/sites/breakingbcs/photos/bcs2-bz-02.webp', '2026-10-27T13:05:00-05:00'::timestamptz, array['housing','building permits','apartments','Census Bureau','real estate']::text[], '• 확인할 점: Figures from Census Bureau BPS metro monthly files cbsamonthly_202609.xls (2026 YTD) and cbsamonthly_202509.xls (2025 YTD as originally reported). Prior-year figures may have been revised in annual data; comparison uses the as-reported Sept. 2025 file.
• 확인할 점: Census monthly metro data partly rely on imputation for non-reporting permit offices and can be revised.
• 확인할 점: Percentages computed by us: 3,254/1,746 = +86.4%; 1,249/1,384 = -9.8%.
• 확인할 점: The 11,000-unit pipeline figure is from the College Station Sept. 10 Terafab presentation summary (city blog, Sept. 15).
• 확인할 점: Texas A&M Real Estate Research Center site blocked automated access (403), so MLS sales data were not used.
• 원문(U.S. Census Bureau — Building Permits Survey, metro monthly units and valuation, September 2026): https://www.census.gov/construction/bps/xls/cbsamonthly_202609.xls
• 원문(U.S. Census Bureau — Building Permits Survey, metro monthly, September 2025): https://www.census.gov/construction/bps/xls/cbsamonthly_202509.xls
• 원문(City of College Station blog — ICYMI Video: The Terafab project''s local impact presented to the City Council (Sept. 15, 2026)): https://blog.cstx.gov/2026/09/15/icymi-video-the-terafab-projects-local-impact-presented-to-the-city-council-sept-10/
• 이용 조건: Text: U.S. federal data (public domain) and city source, rewritten / Photo: CC BY 4.0, Larry D. Moore, File:Tower Crane on Austin High Rise 2020.jpg
• 발행: 대표님 요청으로 승인 대기 없이 바로 발행'),
  ('lifestyle', 'published', 'Halloween Candy Can Sicken Dogs, FDA Warns: Watch for Chocolate and Xylitol', '<p>COLLEGE STATION — Halloween falls on Saturday this year, and while candy bowls fill up across Bryan and College Station, federal regulators say pet owners should keep two common treat ingredients out of their dogs'' reach: chocolate and the sugar substitute xylitol.</p><img src="/sites/breakingbcs/photos/bcs2-ls-08.webp" alt="A dog in a ghost costume next to pumpkins (file photo, 2021; not in the Brazos Valley). Photo: Paige Cody / Unsplash"><p><em>▲ A dog in a ghost costume next to pumpkins (file photo, 2021; not in the Brazos Valley). Photo: Paige Cody / Unsplash</em></p><p>Chocolate contains theobromine and caffeine, stimulants that affect the nervous system and heart, according to the U.S. Food and Drug Administration. Dogs break these down much more slowly than people do, so the effects last longer. Theobromine is the main cause of chocolate poisoning in dogs, the agency says.</p><p>The darker the chocolate, the greater the danger. The FDA estimates that an ounce of unsweetened baking chocolate contains about 364 milligrams of theobromine, compared with about 227 milligrams in dark chocolate, 136 milligrams in semisweet chips and 57 milligrams in milk chocolate. Mild signs can appear at about 9 milligrams per pound of a dog''s body weight and severe signs at about 18 milligrams per pound, the agency says.</p><p>Signs can show up within a few hours and include vomiting, diarrhea, a racing heart, restlessness, increased thirst or urination, muscle spasms and seizures, according to the FDA. Severe cases can be fatal, and the fat and sugar in chocolate can also cause pancreatitis.</p><p>Xylitol, sometimes labeled birch sugar or wood sugar, is found in sugar-free gum and candy, breath mints, some baked goods and some peanut and nut butters, the FDA says. In dogs, it can trigger a rapid release of insulin and a dangerous drop in blood sugar within 10 to 60 minutes. Vomiting often comes first, followed by weakness, staggering, collapse or seizures. Because low blood sugar may not appear for 12 to 24 hours, a dog may need to be watched in an animal hospital.</p><p>The FDA says xylitol does not appear to be as dangerous for cats, which tend not to eat sweets, but ferrets can develop low blood sugar and seizures after eating it.</p><p>The agency advises storing candy where pets cannot get to it and checking labels on sugar-free products. If a dog eats chocolate or a product with xylitol, the FDA says to call a veterinarian, an emergency animal clinic or an animal poison control center right away.</p><p><em>※ This article was written with the help of AI, based on public and official sources.</em></p>', 'Before trick-or-treaters arrive Saturday, the FDA says to keep chocolate and sugar-free treats with xylitol away from dogs. Dark and baking chocolate are the most dangerous.', '/sites/breakingbcs/photos/bcs2-ls-08.webp', '2026-10-27T13:20:00-05:00'::timestamptz, array['Halloween','pets','dogs','pet safety','FDA']::text[], '• 확인할 점: Sources: FDA ''Leave Chocolate Out of Rover''s Celebrations'' (content current as of April 29, 2024) and FDA ''Paws Off Xylitol; It''s Dangerous for Dogs'' (content current as of Dec. 17, 2025).
• 확인할 점: The AVMA Halloween pet safety pages loaded empty for automated access (JavaScript), so AVMA guidance (costumes, glow sticks, decorations, ID tags) was not used. Editor could add it after checking avma.org.
• 확인할 점: Halloween 2026 is Saturday, Oct. 31 (calendar). No local city Halloween events were included: the College Station Halloween page said 2026 events were still being planned, and the haunted hikes found appear to be past or unconfirmed.
• 확인할 점: Theobromine figures are approximate per the FDA. Phone numbers for poison control are left out per style rules.
• 확인할 점: Photo: dog only per Commons description (Tompkins Square Park Halloween dog parade, Oct. 20, 2012); check for people in the background. Author asks for a link to petful.com, which is optional and not included in the caption.
• 원문(FDA — Leave Chocolate Out of Rover''s Celebrations (content current as of April 29, 2024)): https://www.fda.gov/animal-veterinary/animal-health-literacy/leave-chocolate-out-rovers-celebrations
• 원문(FDA — Paws Off Xylitol; It''s Dangerous for Dogs (content current as of Dec. 17, 2025)): https://www.fda.gov/consumers/consumer-updates/paws-xylitol-its-dangerous-dogs
• 이용 조건: Text: original wording based on FDA pages (U.S. federal works, public domain) / Photo: Unsplash License, Paige Cody / Unsplash, https://unsplash.com/photos/a-dog-wearing-a-ghost-costume-next-to-a-pumpkin-29j0KKj2fbg
• 발행: 대표님 요청으로 승인 대기 없이 바로 발행'),
  ('college-station', 'published', 'Food Truck Wednesday Returns to Wolf Pen Creek Oct. 28, Ends Season Nov. 11', '<p>COLLEGE STATION — College Station Parks and Recreation''s Food Truck Wednesday series has two evenings left this fall at the Wolf Pen Creek Festival Site, the first of them on Wednesday, Oct. 28.</p><img src="/sites/breakingbcs/photos/bcs2-cv-08.webp" alt="Food trucks lined up along a walkway (file photo; location not given). It is not College Station&#x27;s Food Truck Wednesday. Photo: Yunus Emre Yazici / Pexels"><p><em>▲ Food trucks lined up along a walkway (file photo; location not given). It is not College Station''s Food Truck Wednesday. Photo: Yunus Emre Yazici / Pexels</em></p><p>The free events run from 5 to 8 p.m., with the final fall date on Nov. 11, according to the schedule the city published Sept. 1. Earlier evenings were held Sept. 9, Sept. 23 and Oct. 14.</p><p>Each night features a rotating lineup of local food trucks, along with music and yard games in Wolf Pen Creek Park, the city said. Admission is free, and food is sold on site.</p><p>The city said the truck lineup is subject to change and that updates are posted on the parks department''s social media accounts the Monday before each event.</p><p>Alcohol and glass containers are not allowed. Free parking is available at the Meyer Senior and Community Center and at Post Oak Mall, with accessible parking near Colgate Drive, according to the city.</p><p>The festival site also hosted the city''s Trunk or Tree-t event with the Texas A&amp;M Forest Service on Oct. 23, which combined Halloween activities with free tree seedlings ahead of Texas Arbor Day on Nov. 6.</p><p><em>※ This article was written with the help of AI, based on public and official sources.</em></p>', 'College Station''s Food Truck Wednesday has two fall dates left at the Wolf Pen Creek Festival Site, Oct. 28 and Nov. 11, with free admission, music and yard games from 5 to 8 p.m.', '/sites/breakingbcs/photos/bcs2-cv-08.webp', '2026-10-27T13:50:00-05:00'::timestamptz, array['College Station','Wolf Pen Creek','Food Truck Wednesday','parks and recreation','events']::text[], '• 확인할 점: Schedule is from the city''s Sept. 1, 2026 blog post; the city says trucks are subject to change. Vendor names deliberately omitted so no business is singled out.
• 확인할 점: Weather cancellations not checked; confirm Oct. 28 event is on before publishing.
• 확인할 점: Trunk or Tree-t (Oct. 23) is described from the Oct. 21 preview; no post-event report was checked. Texas Arbor Day date (Nov. 6) is from the city''s blog, which said Mayor John Nichols would proclaim it at the Oct. 22 council meeting.
• 확인할 점: ls writer has a separate food-dining piece on College Station''s mobile food vendor rules; this story is about the parks event only.
• 확인할 점: Photo: crowd street scene; editor should check for large faces or prominent business signs before publishing.
• 원문(City of College Station — Delicious eats and fall fun are rolling back into the Wolf Pen Creek Festival Site (Sept. 1, 2026)): https://www.cstx.gov/news/posts/delicious-eats-and-fall-fun-are-rolling-back-into-the-wolf-pen-creek-festival-site/
• 원문(City of College Station blog — full schedule post (Sept. 1, 2026)): https://blog.cstx.gov/2026/09/01/delicious-eats-and-fall-fun-are-rolling-back-into-the-wolf-pen-creek-festival-site-this-fall/
• 원문(City of College Station blog — Halloween fun meets Texas Arbor Day at Friday''s Trunk or Tree-t (Oct. 21, 2026)): https://blog.cstx.gov/2026/10/21/halloween-fun-meets-texas-arbor-day-at-fridays-trunk-or-tree-t-at-wolf-pen-creek/
• 이용 조건: Text: facts from City of College Station releases, rewritten / Photo: Pexels License, Yunus Emre Yazici / Pexels, https://www.pexels.com/photo/colorful-food-trucks-lined-up-on-a-sunny-day-37388111/
• 발행: 대표님 요청으로 승인 대기 없이 바로 발행'),
  ('basketball', 'published', 'PJ Haggerty Named to Jerry West Award Preseason Watch List', '<p>COLLEGE STATION — Texas A&amp;M guard PJ Haggerty was named Tuesday to the 20-player preseason watch list for the Jerry West Shooting Guard of the Year Award, the Naismith Basketball Hall of Fame announced, according to Texas A&amp;M Athletics.</p><img src="/sites/breakingbcs/photos/bcs2-sp-05.webp" alt="A basketball on a hardwood court (file photo, 2023; taken in Ontario, Canada, not at Texas A&amp;M, and does not show PJ Haggerty). Photo: LARO Studio / Unsplash"><p><em>▲ A basketball on a hardwood court (file photo, 2023; taken in Ontario, Canada, not at Texas A&amp;M, and does not show PJ Haggerty). Photo: LARO Studio / Unsplash</em></p><p>Haggerty, a 6-foot-4, 195-pound newcomer, came to Texas A&amp;M after one season at Kansas State. He started all 31 games he played there in 2025-26 and averaged 23.4 points, fourth in the nation and second in the Big 12, along with 5.3 rebounds and 3.8 assists, the athletics department said. He scored 30 or more points five times, with a season high of 37 against Mississippi State.</p><p>It is not his first brush with the award. In 2024-25 at Memphis, Haggerty was a top-five finalist for the Jerry West award and a top-15 finalist for the John R. Wooden Award after averaging 21.7 points on 47.6% shooting, with 5.8 rebounds, 3.7 assists and 1.8 steals a game.</p><p>That season he was named American Athletic Conference Player of the Year and a second-team All-American by The Associated Press, the U.S. Basketball Writers Association and The Sporting News, and a third-team All-American by the National Association of Basketball Coaches. Memphis won the AAC regular-season and tournament titles and reached the NCAA Tournament, and Haggerty was invited to the NBA Draft Combine.</p><p>Haggerty began his college career at TCU, where he redshirted in 2022-23, and also played at Tulsa before Memphis, according to the release.</p><p>He was named to the media''s Preseason All-SEC Third Team earlier this month and scored 28 points with four assists and four steals in the Aggies'' exhibition at SMU on Sunday.</p><p>Texas A&amp;M opens the regular season against Alabama State at 7 p.m. Tuesday, Nov. 3, at Reed Arena.</p><p><em>※ This article was written with the help of AI, based on public and official sources.</em></p>', 'Texas A&M newcomer PJ Haggerty, who averaged 23.4 points a game at Kansas State last season, is on the 20-player preseason watch list for the Jerry West Shooting Guard of the Year Award.', '/sites/breakingbcs/photos/bcs2-sp-05.webp', '2026-10-27T14:35:00-05:00'::timestamptz, array['Texas A&M basketball','PJ Haggerty','Jerry West Award','Aggies','Reed Arena']::text[], '• 확인할 점: Commons file ''PJ Haggerty.jpg'' is from Flickr (2C2K Photography, CC BY 2.0, reviewed by FlickreviewR), dated Feb. 2, 2025, categorized under the 2024-25 season; the page does not name the game or team, so the caption does not say which uniform he is wearing — editor should look at the image before publishing.
• 확인할 점: SMU exhibition detail repeats a fact from the earlier tipoff story; it is only one sentence of context.
• 원문(Texas A&M Athletics — Haggerty Named to Jerry West Shooting Guard of the Year Preseason Watch List (Oct. 27, 2026)): https://12thman.com/news/2026/10/27/haggerty-named-to-jerry-west-shooting-guard-of-the-year-preseason-watch-list
• 이용 조건: Text: facts from Texas A&M Athletics (12thman.com) releases, rewritten; quotes as published by the athletics department / Photo: Unsplash License, LARO Studio / Unsplash, https://unsplash.com/photos/2D4QoJ0Z--A
• 발행: 대표님 요청으로 승인 대기 없이 바로 발행')
) as v(section, status, title, body, excerpt, thumb, published_at, tags, notes)
join categories c on c.outlet_id = ctx.outlet_id and c.slug = v.section
where not exists (select 1 from articles a where a.outlet_id = ctx.outlet_id and a.title = v.title);

-- 확인 (섹션별 기사 수·상태·기자명)
select c.name as "섹션", a.byline as "기자명", a.status as "상태", count(*) as "기사 수"
from articles a join categories c on c.id = a.category_id join outlets o on o.id = a.outlet_id
where o.name = 'Breaking BCS'
group by 1, 2, 3 order by 1;
